# Blazor Component Conventions

- Component packages use `<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">`, target `net10.0` only, add `<FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App"/>`, and reference `MudBlazor` (version-less, via CPM).
- UI is MudBlazor-first (`MudCard`, `MudGrid`, `MudDataGrid`, `MudAlert`, ...). Reuse shared building blocks from `Lyo.Net/Integration/Web/Lyo.Web.Components` (`LyoDataGrid`, `LyoForm`, `LyoFormInput`, `LyoFileUpload`, `JsonEditor`, `LyoChip`, ...) before writing new primitives; generic reusable components carry the `Lyo` prefix.
- If a UI pattern is used in more than one place, or looks like it will be (timestamps, ids, truncated text, status chips, duration, …), extract a shared `Lyo*` component or helper in `Lyo.Web.Components` instead of copying MudBlazor markup. Examples: `LyoTimestamp`, `LyoIdField`, `LyoTruncatedText`, `LyoChip` / `LyoChips`. Domain packages keep only domain color/icon maps (`JobColorHelper`, `ReportColorHelper`, `SmsColorHelper`, `CacheColorHelper`); rendering goes through the shared primitive.
- Dialog headers: title text stays on the first row with the debug / close buttons. Status chips go in `LyoDialog.TitleChips` (a wrap row under the header, above the body). Do not put chips in `TitleContent` — they collide with the header buttons.
- Do not extract one-off editor chrome: `LyoChipInput`, `MudChipSet` children, filter-builder presets, and similar controls that must stay a real `MudChip`.
- Each package has an `_Imports.razor` collecting all `@using` directives (alphabetical) and optionally a `GlobalUsings.cs` for C# usings.
- Small components keep an inline `@code { ... }` block; complex components split logic into a `partial class` code-behind (`Component.razor.cs`) — see `Lyo.Web.Components/DataGrid/LyoDataGrid.razor.cs`.
- Required inputs use `[Parameter] [EditorRequired]`. Data access flows through an `IApiClient` passed as a parameter (or cascading) rather than injecting concrete services; `@inject` is fine for `ILogger<T>` and UI services (`IDialogService`, `ISnackbar`).
- Private state fields use `_camelCase`; collection defaults use collection expressions (`= [];`).
- Razor markup uses same-line braces for `@if`/`@foreach` blocks (matching existing components), and early `return;` inside markup to short-circuit loading/empty states.
- Export/grid integrations go through `Lyo.Web.Components.Export` (+ `.Csv`/`.Xlsx`) rather than bespoke export code.
